WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.790
(bright music)

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:06.553
- I see my work as woven
into the fabric of cities.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:13.440
These soft fibers move and
adapt to wind and light and rain,

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.259
and they are a way of being;

00:00:18.259 --> 00:00:20.763
they are about interconnectedness.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.120
I'm Janet Echelman, I'm an artist.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:35.120
I bring sculpture and form and
light into the public realm,

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:40.040
so that we can literally change the spaces

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.543
that we live in, in cities.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.600
My sculpture has traveled
to five continents.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.610
It takes an incredible team to create

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.250
one of these sculptures.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:56.800
I am working with computer
scientists and artisans,

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.980
and aeronautical and structural engineers

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.433
all over the world.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.662
This part is hanging the
way we want it to hang,

00:01:06.662 --> 00:01:07.630
down there.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:11.620
My studio is where we incubate ideas.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:16.620
Some of my newest work I'm
using data sets from science,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:21.770
whether it's human action or
an earthquake and tsunami,

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:26.370
to reveal our relationship with the world;

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.460
and then I just start sketching,

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:31.483
whether it's with a pen or paintbrush.

00:01:32.693 --> 00:01:34.960
Then we start to model
it in three dimensions

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:38.303
in the computer, and we
also make physical models.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:44.820
They begin as raw fiber that
is braided into twine and rope,

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:50.530
put on to bobbins, and
loomed using machines,

00:01:50.530 --> 00:01:54.050
and the ropes are spliced by hand.

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:57.420
To take the work and
install it in the city

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:00.940
is a whole 'nother set of artistry.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:02.690
The peace comes together as

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:06.123
a single sewn garment for the city.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:12.970
My work is about the
dynamic nature of life,

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:15.410
and it's always unfolding.

00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:19.060
During the day the colors of the sculpture

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:23.000
change slightly as sunlight changes.

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:26.270
At night I'm projecting colored light

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:29.843
that is very slowly, gradually changing.

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:33.080
It's never the same piece,

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:35.950
and you and the person
you come to see it with

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:39.470
might have completely
different experiences.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:43.103
The work invites people to engage with it.

